# The pictures of wrap.md: a cylinder turned from a rectangle about its
# lower side, a rectangle drawn in a workplane through the cylinder's
# axis and wrapped onto it, raised then sunk; then the wrap example's
# handle.
cursor on
key r
move 250 200
down L 250 200
up L 250 200
move 350 250
down L 350 250
up L 350 250
key esc
move 300 250
down L 300 250
up L 300 250
key l shift
key esc
view rotated
menu View|Zoom To Fit
menu View|Zoom Out
cursor off
shot wrap-1-lathed gw
# A workplane at the rectangle's corner, parallel to XY: it holds the
# axis, so it is parallel to it.
view default
move 250 200
down L 250 200
up L 250 200
key w shift
view default
menu View|Show|Construction Entities
cursor on
key r
move 262 212
down L 262 212
up L 262 212
move 330 236
down L 330 236
up L 330 236
key esc
menu View|Show|Construction Entities
move 420 330
mark 254 204 84 40
shot wrap-2-sketch
menu View|Show|Selectable Faces
click-face face 4 of g003-lathe
shot wrap-3-face gw
menu Features|Wrap Sketch Onto Face
view rotated
menu View|Zoom To Fit
menu View|Zoom Out
cursor off
shot wrap-4-raised
cursor on
twmove 125 165
mark 116 162 70 22 tw
shot wrap-5-sunk-link tw
twdown L 125 165
twup L 125 165
cursor off
shot wrap-6-sunk gw
file $repo/examples/scripts/wrap/wrap.go
answer no
menu File|New
menu Script|Run File...
view rotated
menu View|Zoom To Fit
menu View|Zoom Out
shot wrap-7-handle gw
